Description: use registered freedesktop categories in the desktop entry
 The entry listed "09-sniffing-spoofing", which is a Kali menu category and not
 one of the registered main or additional categories in the freedesktop menu
 specification, so desktop-file-validate and lintian both reject it. Keep the
 intent by moving it to an X- vendor extension, which the specification allows,
 and add the registered Network and Security categories so the entry lands
 somewhere sensible on a plain Debian desktop too.
Author: Kevin Amorin <kamorin@gmail.com>
Forwarded: not-needed
Last-Update: 2026-08-01
--- a/packaging/dhcpig-web.desktop
+++ b/packaging/dhcpig-web.desktop
@@ -6,5 +6,5 @@
 Exec=pkexec dhcpig-web --open
 Icon=dhcpig
 Terminal=true
-Categories=09-sniffing-spoofing;Network;Security;
+Categories=Network;Security;X-Kali-09-sniffing-spoofing;
 Keywords=dhcp;pentest;exhaustion;scapy;arp;fingerprint;
